# Settings::strictness — the evidence behind the Strict default — 2026-08-28

Host:      dev (AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D, 32 threads, 60 GiB), Ubuntu, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
Base:      origin/main @ 00ad667 (docs: farm-artifact triage record — #430/#436/#439 …)
Branch:    feat/strictness (this record's commit)
Toolchain: stable (release, default features) for everything below
Oracles:   aomdec from libaom 632172a (~/work/aom/build_dbg), dav1d 1.5.3 CLI
           (~/work/dav1d-ref/build, `--strict 0` = library default, `--strict 1`)

Everything below is output from a command run on this box. Nothing is estimated.


## 1. The two streams behind the issues

Both are raw OBU streams; aomdec needs an IVF wrapper (one frame = the whole
stream, `python3 ivfwrap.py`), dav1d's CLI likewise.

    stream                                        bytes  aomdec                          dav1d --strict 0   dav1d --strict 1
    tests/strictness_vectors/
      segment_id_desync_zenrav1e35.obu   (#422)   4267   "Corrupted segment_ids"         decodes 1/1        rejects (EINVAL)
      tile_padding_desync_fuzz424.obu    (#424)  13213   "Failed to decode tile data"    decodes 1/1        rejects (EINVAL)

#424's farm artifact (sha256 d204fcaa…, 13278 bytes, block storage
/mnt/v/fuzzes/rav1d-safe/differential/) carries a fourth OBU of garbage after
the frame OBU that even lenient dav1d rejects (EINVAL after emitting the frame);
the committed vector is cut at the frame OBU's end (offset 13213) and keeps every
verdict above.

rav1d-safe on unmodified main (examples/crash_sweep, 4 entry points incl.
production defaults): both streams "decoded a frame", 0 panics — i.e. the
pre-change decoder concealed both, exactly like dav1d --strict 0.

With this branch (tests/strictness.rs, 5 tests, 0.02 s):

    Strictness::Lenient   #422 -> Ok(192x256 frame)     #424 -> Ok(10-bit frame)
    Strictness::Strict    #422 -> Err(InvalidData)      #424 -> Err(InvalidData)
    Settings::default()   == Strict
    strict_std_compliance = true (deprecated)  -> behaves as Strict
    kodim03_yuv420_8bpc.obu (conforming control): identical luma under both

What each level is, mechanically:

    Lenient  dav1d library default (strict_std_compliance = 0).
    Strict   Rav1dContext.strict_std_compliance = true (every check dav1d gates on
             it: OBU trailing bits, tile symbol-decoder padding
             (check_trailing_bits_after_symbol_coder), forbidden bit, zero
             timing_info, intra_only + refresh 0xff, show_existing of a
             non-showable frame, identity MC with subsampled chroma, frame-thread
             reference-error propagation) PLUS the AV1 §6.10.8 segment_id bound in
             decode_b (both the pre-skip and post-skip read_segment_id sites).
             Spec text (5.11.9 / 6.10.8, extracted from the spec PDF):
               "It is a requirement of bitstream conformance that the postprocessed
                value of segment_id (i.e. the value returned by neg_deinterleave) is
                in the range 0 to LastActiveSegId (inclusive of endpoints)."
             libaom decodemv.c read_segment_id(): aom_internal_error(…,
             "Corrupted segment_ids"). dav1d decode.c: `b->seg_id = 0; // error?`.
             The spec initialises LastActiveSegId = 0; dav1d keeps -1 for "no
             active feature", so the strict bound is max(last_active_segid, 0).

The symbol-decoder over-read check (msac.cnt <= -15 at the end of every tile
sbrow) was ALREADY unconditional in dav1d/rav1d-safe and is exactly libaom's
aom_reader_has_overflowed() (spec 8.2.4: SymbolMaxBits >= -14). It is not
part of this change; #424's stream trips the tile-padding check, not this one.


## 2. Cost of the Strict default on conforming / real content

### 2a. dav1d md5 conformance gate, Settings::default() (now Strict)

    $ cargo test --release --test decode_md5_verify
    test result: ok. 14 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored   (25.77 s)
    (766 vectors across 8-bit data/intra/features/issues/quantizer/vq, 10-bit, 12-bit)

Unchanged from main. No dav1d test vector — including the 8-bit/issues set —
trips any Strict check.

### 2b. Real AVIF/OBU corpora, examples/strictness_sweep.rs (Lenient vs Strict)

    $ strictness_sweep --jobs 4 --quiet ~/work/codec-corpus ~/work/zen/zenavif/tests \
        test-vectors/bench tests/crash_vectors fuzz/regression
    389 files (34 unreadable: non-AV1 primary items / non-AVIF), 8 disagreements
             lenient |   frame   nofrm   error  <- strict
               frame |     315       0       8
               nofrm |       0      19       0
               error |       0       0      13

    The 8: codec-corpus/avif-conformance/invalid/corrupted_mdat.avif (a
    deliberately corrupted conformance-suite sample — the one real file, and the
    right verdict) + 7 fuzz-derived crash repros from tests/crash_vectors and
    fuzz/regression (mutated streams; see §3 for what that means for the gate).
    Every other real file: identical verdict.

    $ run-heavy --mem 16G --jobs 4 -- strictness_sweep --jobs 4 --quiet /mnt/v/input/zensim
    53484 files (0 unreadable), 0 disagreements
             lenient |   frame   nofrm   error  <- strict
               frame |   53484       0       0
    run-heavy: done rc=0 448s | peak-RSS 0.13GiB | min-avail 40829MiB | peak-load 7.85

    /mnt/v/input/zensim = the zensim synthetic-v2 AVIF encodes (images/,
    scale-pyramid/, spike-{lanczos3,mitchell,triangle}/, text-ui/, sources*/;
    59 GB, 706 files over 1 MB). 106,968 decodes, every one a frame under both.


## 3. Fuzz plumbing consequences

decode_obu and parse_seq_header now pin Strictness::Lenient (maximal reach);
differential_dav1d compares strict-vs-strict (see
differential_triage_2026-08-28.meta). tests/fuzz_regression.rs mirrors them and gained a FIFTH
entry point, `default_lenient`: production defaults are now Strict and reject
7 mutated seeds before the kernel they guard (§2b) — with only the old four
entry points the reach floor dropped 21 -> 20:

    only 20 of 33 seeds decoded a frame, expected at least 21   (before the 5th entry point)
    $ cargo test --release --test fuzz_regression
    test result: ok. 3 passed   (with it; MIN_SEEDS_REACHING_RECON unchanged at 21)

examples/crash_sweep.rs mirrors the same five.


